<article class="env-lemma" id="0CV4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CV4">Lemma <span data-tag="0CV4">71.4.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $i : Z \to X$ be a finite morphism. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ Z$-module. Then $\text{WeakAss}_{X/Y}(i_*\mathcal{G}) = i(\text{WeakAss}_{Z/Y}(\mathcal{G}))$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the case of schemes (Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/0CUD" data-tag="0CUD">31.8.3</a>) by étale localization. Details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>